<table border="0" cellpadding="5" width="550" cellspacing="5" height="400" >
<tr valign="top" height="400" >
<td tEditID="c1r1" style=" background-color:#FFFFFF; bEditID:r3st1; color:#000000; bLabel:main; font-size:12pt; font-family:arial;" aEditID="c1r1" locked="0" >
<![CDATA[<font face="arial" style="font-size: 12pt;">Dear&nbsp;{!Contact.FirstName},</font><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><br></div><div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial">Thank you for application for admission to the Herberger Institute School of Music at Arizona State University. We are pleased to inform you that you have been invited for a live audition/interview as a result of your prescreening submission. At this time we cannot schedule an on-campus audition because you are missing the following items from your application:</font></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><ul><li>Transcripts - INSTITUTION</li><li>Proof of English Proficiency</li><li>English Proficiency Exemption</li><li>Letters of Recommendation</li></ul></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><b>Transcripts</b>: Transcripts must be sealed and sent from the registrar’s office of each university attended. All international transcripts music be submitted in the original language accompanied by an official English translation. You may not complete your own translation. Electronic copies are NOT accepted and must be delivered to the address listed below.&nbsp;</font></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial">Please send official transcripts, to the following address:</font></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><b>If sending by U.S. Mail:</b></font></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial">Arizona State University</font></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial">Graduate Admission Services</font></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;">PO Box 871003</div><div style="font-size: 12pt;">Tempe, AZ 85287-1003</div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><br></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><b>If sending by FedEx, DHL or UPS:</b></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Graduate Admission Services</span></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;">Arizona State University</div><div style="font-size: 12pt;">1151 S. Forest Avenue, #SSV 112</div><div style="font-size: 12pt;">Tempe, AZ 85287-0112</div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><br></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><b>Proof of English Proficiency:</b>&nbsp;An audition cannot be scheduled without proof that you have met English proficiency. You may meet English proficiency by the following tests:</span></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><ul><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">TOEFL: score of at least 550 (PBT) or 80 (iBT).</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">IELTS: overall band score of at least 3.5.</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Pearson Test of English (PTE): score of at least 60</span></li></ul></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;">**You must pass the exam after August 1, 2014 for Fall admission and January 1, 2014 for Spring 2016 admission.**</span><span class="Apple-tab-span" style="font-size: 12pt; white-space: pre;">	</span></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><br></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial">Please send official test scores for English Proficiency electronically. ASU’s institutional code is 4007.</font></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><br></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><b>Proof of English Proficiency Exemption</b>: You may qualify for the English proficiency exemption if you have met the following:</font></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><br></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;">1. Successfully complete the highest level at the American English and Culture Program (AECP) with grades of B or better.</div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><br></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;">OR<br><br></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;">2. Attend in-person a regionally accredited college or university in the United States and meet onf of the following conditions:</div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><ul><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Earned a bachelor’s degree or higher in the US, or</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Completed at least 12 hours of graduate coursework with a cumulative GPA of 3.0 on a 4.0 scale, or</span></li><li><span style="font-size: 12pt;">Completed at least 90 credit hours of undergraduate coursework with a cumulative GPA of 3.0 on a 4.0 scale.</span></li></ul></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><b>Letters of Recommendation</b>: Letters are completed by your references listed in your School of Music Application through DecisionDesk. Please login to your account&nbsp;<a href="https://app.decisiondesk.com/login">here</a>&nbsp;to determine which letters you are missing.&nbsp;</span></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><span style="font-size: 12pt;"><br></span></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial">We will confirm your audition/interview date once all above items have been received. Please bear in mind that audition/interview dates are filling quickly and that your desired date may not be available if there is a further delay in the submission of your outstanding items.&nbsp;</font></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial">If you have any questions about the above items mentioned, please contact&nbsp;<a href="mailto:musicadmissions@asu.edu">musicadmissions@asu.edu</a>. Thank you for your interest in studying in the Herberger Institute School of Music. We look forward to receiving your missing application items and scheduling your audition.&nbsp;</font></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial">Sincerely,</font></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><br></font></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial">ASU School of Music in the Herberger Institute for Design and the Arts</font></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial">Office of Admissions</font></div><div style="font-size: 12pt;"><font face="arial"><a href="mailto:musicadmissions@asu.edu">MusicAdmissions@asu.edu</a></font></div></div><div><br></div>]]></td>
</tr>
</table>